schema: test/v2
level: epic
epic: E-GATETRUTH
tests:
  e2e:
    count: 12
    what: "This epic wrote one: tests/e2e_gate_truth.rs (1) - the epic e2e, composing all four fixes at one seam over a hermetic temp repo through the real xtask binary, the real pre-merge-commit hook and real git. A WU adds a component, retires its design per DEC-16 and cites it at the bytes the build read (P1/DEC-28, judged at its last state per DEC-29); the mr commit that lands its report reports landing, not error: (P2a); the report is link-checked red then green (P2b); the merge is refused for a signer this checkout does not list, naming the signer and the roster, then accepted for a listed one (P3). Each WU deferred this step in identical words; it is paid here. Regression proof: against an xtask built at the epic base 1c8d587 it reds at exactly P1 (does not resolve at the tip), P3 (no valid mr/v1 note) and P2b (ungoverned, not checked). Touched: tests/e2e_manual_review.rs (1, E-NMWF) - re-run green after both gate e2es moved to the shared harness. Unchanged and re-run, proxy-behaviour e2es from earlier epics: tests/e2e_capture.rs (6), tests/e2e_h2.rs (4). Additionally, outside this 513-test run: xtask/tests/e2e_design_flow.rs (5, --features design-e2e), whose a_build_that_adds_a_surface_cites_the_design_it_read W2 extended with the retired-design citation case."
  integration:
    count: 199
    what: "This epic wrote or extended four: xtask/tests/mr.rs (58) - P2a and P3, including a commit that lands reporting success and no error, a first commit from an unborn HEAD, a signed note whose signer this checkout lists no key for naming the signer and the roster, and a genuine two-worktree test (worktree A signs, worktree B has no roster) proving the DEC-10 layout is the cause the message must name. xtask/tests/dod_gate.rs (82) - the citation predicate at the seam: green on the legal add-build-retire history, red on a fabricated path and on a blob no commit held, the DEC-29 retired-design artifact join, and the two design_scope tests that hold the design_artifacts_with de-duplication behaviour-preserving. xtask/tests/verify_doc.rs (16) - P2b: a dead relative href reds a governed doc and an ungoverned one, but not a draft, an archived doc or a docs/.archive/ link, plus a run over this repo own docs, itself now a test. tests/dod_hooks.rs (12) - the hook dispatch. Unchanged and re-run: tests/api.rs (11), xtask/tests/doc_hooks.rs (8), xtask/tests/gate0_cache.rs (5), tests/ca.rs (3), tests/worktree_setup_hook.rs (2), xtask/tests/ui.rs (2)."
  unit:
    count: 302
    what: "xtask/src (237) and src (65) library unit tests. This epic added coverage for the citation predicate widened through history, last_state and added_under, the retired-design artifact join, git_env/git_outcome error formatting and the commit verdict, the Authorisation enum three states, and the href resolver path handling."
suite: "513 tests green across 20 suites (cargo test --workspace --features hook-tests) - 12 e2e + 199 integration + 302 unit, which sums to 513. Unchanged across the review-fix refactor. The feature-gated design-e2e suite (5 tests) is additional and not in that figure. clippy --workspace --all-targets clean under pedantic with -D warnings."
counts_verified: "every figure read from per-suite cargo test output at this tip, and the three tiers checked to sum to the stated total. Two earlier drafts of this note were wrong and both were caught by the epic review: the first transposed dod_gate.rs (82) with the trawler unit suite (65) and understated integration by 98; the second omitted tests/e2e_capture.rs (6) and tests/e2e_h2.rs (4) from every tier, so its tiers summed to 503 against a stated 513."
review_fixes: "the epic tip carries three review fixes (987ca86): the two gate e2es share tests/common/gitrepo.rs, design_scope walks history once via design_artifacts_with, and an .eq(&false) became a negation. Their coverage is the two design_scope tests plus both e2es re-run green; the unit tier is waived for that commit alone - it removes a duplicate walk and extracts an existing harness, adding no behaviour a new unit test could assert. The harness carries #![allow(dead_code)] because each test compiles the module separately and e2e_manual_review does not call three of its methods; removing the allow was tried and reds."
